# HAMIN — "The Things You Notice"
# Route theme: being noticed. Romance through small acts of attention, not declarations.
# Speech: polite (KO 존댓말 / JA です・ます) until the SPEECH SHIFT inside hamin_room; casual after.
# Seeds used: var.drink (prologue vending machine), flag.cold (prologue "Are you cold?").
# Running details: the laundromat song, corn tea, 2:47 (the laugh's timestamp), "next time", eight cups.

=== hamin_intro
@show hamin neutral at=c
@cam closeup hamin
> Hamin is standing by the front desk holding a roll of paper towels he did not have ten minutes ago.
> He tears off three squares, folds them once, and sets them on the sofa arm beside Charlie, whose hair is still dripping onto an old flyer.
@show charlie surprised at=l
charlie: Oh. Thanks. Wait, where did you even find these?
hamin: Staff bathroom. Second shelf.
charlie: How do you know there's a staff bathroom?
hamin: The door says "staff".
charlie[laugh]: Okay. Yeah. That tracks.
@hide charlie
> Justin drifts past behind the sofa, lifts a packet of crackers out of Hyunjun's jacket pocket without breaking stride, and keeps drifting.
hamin: He hasn't eaten since lunch. Hyunjun knows. That's why he always buys two.
> He says it quietly, to nobody in particular. Then he looks at you, and then, briefly, at the empty can you still haven't found a bin for.
@if var.drink == "peach"
    hamin: Peach iced tea. In the rain.
    hamin: That's very brave.
@elif var.drink == "choco"
    hamin: Hot chocolate. Good choice.
    hamin: You were holding it through your sleeve. It must have been very hot.
@elif var.drink == "coffee"
    hamin: Black coffee. At one in the morning.
    hamin: So you're planning to stay up.
@else
    hamin: Grape soda.
    hamin: I didn't know anyone actually bought those. I thought they were for decoration.
* [playful] "Do you always take inventory of people?"
    @rel hamin closeness+1
    hamin[smile]: Only the ones holding cans.
    hamin: The bin is behind the desk, by the way. Under the lost property box.
* [sincere] "You noticed that?"
    @rel hamin trust+1
    hamin[shy]: It's a habit. Sorry.
    hamin: The bin is behind the desk. If you were looking for it.
* [quiet] Hand him the can, since he seems to know where it goes.
    @rel hamin closeness+1
    > He takes it without comment and drops it into a bin behind the desk that you would never have found.
    hamin: …I do know where it goes.
@if flag.cold
    hamin: There's a heater under the window. It works if you hit the side twice.
    hamin: I hit it. It's on now. Just so you know.
you: Did you send something here too? To the Future Letter Project?
hamin[thinking]: I think so.
hamin: I think I sent the sea.
> He says it the way other people say *a postcard*.
hamin: A recording. From Busan. I was fourteen. It seemed like a good idea at the time.
hamin: I don't really remember why.
> He remembers exactly why. You can tell by how quickly he looks at the Archive Wall and then away from it.
hamin: Also — you were humming. At the door, earlier.
you: Was I?
hamin: The song from the laundromat. It's been playing the same one on a loop since we got here. Probably since two thousand and ten.
hamin[shy]: …Sorry. I notice things. I'm not keeping a list.
> He is, you suspect, keeping a list.
@hub act1

=== hamin_intro_repeat
@show hamin neutral at=c
hamin: The heater's still on. Charlie's mostly dry.
hamin: Justin has eaten one cracker. That's progress.
> He delivers it like a weather report. It is, somehow, the most reassuring thing anyone has said tonight.
@hub act1

=== hamin_door
@bg studio_hall t=fade d=1.2
@amb none
> The second-floor hallway hums. Eight doors, each with light moving behind the frosted glass.
> Downstairs, Daniel is losing an argument with the claw machine. It sounds like a long argument.
> Behind Hamin's, the light rises and falls, slowly. Like breathing. Like something coming in and going out.
@show hamin neutral at=c
hamin: That one's mine. I think.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 02 — OWNER: HAMIN. STATUS: SEALED. AWAITING CONSENT.
@textbox normal
hamin: It's just the sea. Four minutes of it.
hamin: You might be bored. I'm telling you in advance, so you can't say I didn't warn you.
hamin: If it's boring, you can leave halfway. I won't notice.
> He will notice.
> He isn't looking at the door. He's looking at the floor in front of it, where the light pools and pulls back.
hamin[thinking]: It's fine. You can open it.
hamin: …That sounded like I was talking to a dentist.
hamin: What I mean is, I'd like you to be there. If you want to be.
* [sincere] "Open it."
    @goto hamin_room
* [careful] "Not yet."
    @rel hamin trust+1
    hamin: Okay.
    > He lets out a breath. It isn't quite a laugh.
    hamin[smile]: Honestly, that's a relief. I was going to pretend to be calm for another ten minutes.
    hamin: It's waited six years. It can wait a little longer.
    @hub act2

=== hamin_room
@bg mem_beach t=memory d=2.2
@music hamin
@amb ocean
@fx waves n=1
@cam reveal
> The door opens onto sand.
> Not a picture of sand. Sand, or ECHO's best guess at it — cool and fine, giving a little under each step. The hallway is gone behind you.
> A beach at night. A long curve of dark water, a line of foam that keeps arriving, and far along the shore, the lights of a city that isn't Seoul.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 02 — OWNER: HAMIN. TYPE: VOICE MEMO. LENGTH: FOUR MINUTES, TWELVE SECONDS.
echo: LOCATION: A BEACH IN BUSAN. DATE: JULY, SIX YEARS AGO. 23:41.
echo: UNRESOLVED SUBJECTS: 1.
@textbox normal
@show hamin neutral at=c
