    hamin[shy]: …Thank you. Really.
* [quiet] Stand beside him at the edge and look at the water.
    @rel hamin trust+1
    > He doesn't say anything. After a moment his shoulders come down half an inch, as if he'd been holding them up for both of you.
@textbox echo
echo: Beginning reconstruction. Please do not step on the owner.
@textbox normal
@hide all
@sfx wave
@fx memory n=0.8
@textbox memory
> The light shifts. The moon moves a few degrees along the sky, as if someone nudged it with one finger.
> Up the beach, a boy of fourteen sits cross-legged on the sand, holding a phone out towards the water at arm's length. Very seriously.
> He is trying not to breathe too loudly. You can tell. His whole back is concentrating.
> Thirty metres further along, there is a shape made of soft light. Knees pulled up. Arms around them. Shivering.
> The unresolved subject.
> The boy looks at the phone. Then at the shape. Then at the phone again, like he's trying to work out which one is his problem.
> He stops the recording. He stands up. He walks — not to the shape, but past it, up to the vending machine by the seawall.
@sfx vending
@sfx can
> When he comes back, he is holding a can. He holds it out at arm's length, exactly the way he held the phone.
hamin: Here.
you: …Oh. Thanks?
hamin: It's hot. Corn tea. It was the only hot one.
you: It's July.
hamin: You're shivering. In July.
you: I didn't know the sea got cold at night. We only moved here last week.
you: I thought beaches were a daytime thing.
hamin: It's a night thing too. Just a different one.
> He sits down — not next to the light, but a polite metre away. He presses record again. He doesn't explain.
you: What are you recording?
hamin: The sea.
you: Why?
hamin: I might go to Seoul. Next year, maybe. It's a long story.
hamin: There's no sea in Seoul.
> The light holds the can in both hands and doesn't drink it. For a while there is only the water.
you: It's louder at night. The sea.
hamin: It's the same.
hamin: Everything else is quieter.
you: This is nice. Thank you. It's not my favourite, though.
hamin: …You're reviewing a free drink.
you: I'm just saying. For the record.
hamin: What is your favourite, then?
@if var.drink == "peach"
    you: Peach iced tea.
    hamin: You're shivering. And your favourite drink comes with ice.
    you: It's a summer drink. It's summer.
    hamin: It's summer for everyone except you.
@elif var.drink == "choco"
    you: Hot chocolate. I checked the machine already. It's sold out.
