> The phone, still held very carefully towards the sea, catches every bit of it.
hamin: …
hamin: Next time, then.
you: Next time what?
hamin: That one. The machine doesn't have it. So. Next time.
> From the top of the seawall, a voice calls a name. It comes through as a smear of static — the one word ECHO has never been able to resolve.
