=== hamin_hub
@if flag.room_hamin and not flag.hamin_postchat
    @show hamin smile at=c
    > Hamin is sitting on the arm of the lobby sofa with one earbud in. When he sees you, he takes it out.
    hamin: I was checking it was still on there. The recording.
    hamin: It is. ECHO didn't eat it. I thought it might keep it. It seemed to like it.
    @show daniel laugh at=l
    daniel: Wait. Wait wait wait. Did he just talk to you normally?
    @if rooms() <= 6
        daniel: It's not even three! I said three! Who did it? Was it me? It was me, right?
    @else
        daniel: I said three a.m.! I was basically right! Who did it? Was it me? It was me, right?
    hamin: It wasn't you.
    daniel[laugh]: I'm counting it anyway.
    @hide daniel
    > Daniel wanders off to tell Songha, who can be heard saying he doesn't care, in the voice of someone who cares a little.
    hamin: He's going to tell everyone.
    hamin: That's fine. It's fine. I'm going to go and stand in a different room for a while.
    > He doesn't go anywhere. He moves the earbud from one hand to the other.
    hamin: I listened to it again. Just now. It's different, knowing whose it is.
    you: Different how?
    hamin[thinking]: Before, it was a laugh. Now it's you laughing at me.
    hamin[smile]: Which is worse. And better. Mostly better.
    * [playful] "Did you just skip straight to two forty-seven?"
        @rel hamin closeness+1
        hamin: I skipped to two forty-five. I'm not an animal. You need the run-up.
    * [sincere] "How are you? Actually."
        @rel hamin trust+1
        hamin: Actually?
        hamin: Like I've been holding my breath since I was fourteen and someone just told me I could stop.
        hamin: …That's too much. Forget that. I'm fine. I'm good.
        you: I'm not forgetting it.
        hamin[shy]: No. I didn't think you would.
    * [romantic] Take the earbud he's been passing from hand to hand. {if hamin.closeness >= 3}
        @rel hamin romance+1 closeness+1
        > You hold out your hand. He looks at it, and then puts the earbud in your palm like it might be the wrong thing to hand someone.
        @sfx wave
        > The sea, very small, in one ear. The lobby, very ordinary, in the other. He leans in just enough to share the cord.
        hamin: Two forty-five. Wait for it.
        > You wait for it. So does he. Neither of you is listening to the sea at all.
    @flag hamin_postchat
@elif flag.room_hamin
    @show hamin smile at=c
    @if rooms() >= 6
        hamin: Everyone's eaten now. I checked. Even Songha, and he lied about it twice.
        hamin: You haven't. There's half a kimbap on the desk with your name on it. Literally. I wrote it.
    @else
        hamin: I'm still here. The recording's still there.
        hamin: …I just wanted to say something to you without a reason. That's the reason.
@else
    @show hamin neutral at=c
    hamin: Have you eaten anything?
    hamin: You had a drink. That isn't dinner. I'm only saying.
    @if rooms() >= 2
        hamin: Hyunjun has a bag of crackers. I'll ask him. He'll say yes to me. He says yes to anyone who asks nicely.
    @else
        hamin: Hyunjun has a bag of crackers. Justin has most of them. I'll negotiate.
    > He is already turning towards the other side of the lobby, the way someone turns towards a task they've been waiting for.
    hamin: …My door is the one that sounds like the sea. When you're ready. There's no hurry.
@hub act2

=== hamin_route
@chapter route
@time 03:50
@var route = "hamin"
@bg studio_lounge t=fade d=1.4
@amb room
@music quiet
@cam wide
> Seventy minutes left. The building seems to know it. The lights on the stairs have started dimming one landing at a time, like someone going round switching things off early.
> You find Hamin on the third floor, in the lounge that was a café for about a year, until the espresso machine died and nobody could afford to revive it.
> The machine is still here. So is a kettle, which works.
> And, as of tonight, a row of paper cups on the counter, lined up with a precision that is almost funny.
@show hamin neutral at=c
> Each cup has a name on it in marker. He's filling them with barley tea, one by one, to exactly the same line.
> CHARLIE (ATE NOTHING). JUSTIN (ATE HYUNJUN'S). HYUNJUN (BOUGHT TWO, GAVE ONE AWAY). SONGHA (SAID HE ATE. DIDN'T).
> Yours just says {{playerName}}. Spelled right. You never spelled it for him.
hamin[smile]: Oh. Hi. Yours is the fourth one.
hamin: It's barley tea. I wanted to make toast, but the toaster's already in a box for the renovation crew.
> You count the cups. Then you count them again.
you: There are eight cups.
hamin: Yes.
you: There are nine of us.
hamin: I counted. Twice.
you: Count again.
> He counts. He touches each cup lightly as he goes, the way teachers count heads on a school trip. He gets to the end, and stops.
hamin[surprised]: …Oh.
hamin[thinking]: I didn't count me.
hamin: That's sort of the whole problem, isn't it. In one row of cups.
* [sincere] Take a ninth cup from the stack, write HAMIN on it, and fill it.
    @rel hamin trust+1 romance+1
    > You write his name. Under it, after a moment's thought: (ATE NOTHING. COUNTED TO EIGHT TWICE).
    > He reads it. He reads it again. He puts his hand over his mouth, which is how you learn he does that when he's trying not to laugh.
    hamin[laugh]: That's slander.
    you: Is it wrong?
    hamin: …No.
* [playful] "Eight cups. Very efficient. Very sad."
    @rel hamin closeness+1
    hamin[laugh]: It's not sad. It's a rounding error.
    you: You rounded yourself down to zero.
    hamin: …Okay, when you say it like that, it's a bit sad.
* [quiet] Pour half your tea into a spare cup and slide it across to him.
    @rel hamin trust+1 closeness+1
    > He looks at the cup, then at you, then at the cup, like it's a trick question he wants to get right.
    hamin: Now you've got half.
    you: Now we've both got half.
    hamin[shy]: …That's worse maths and a better answer.
@show charlie surprised at=l
charlie: Wait, what's happening? Is that tea? Is one of those mine?
hamin: The one that says "Charlie".
charlie: It says "Charlie, ate nothing".
hamin: Is it wrong?
